{
  "an7.43:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 7.43 ",
  "an7.43:0.2": "4. Deities ",
  "an7.43:0.3": "Graduation (2nd) ",
  "an7.43:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "an7.43:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Kosambī in Ghosita’s monastery. ",
  "an7.43:1.3": "Then Venerable Ānanda robed up in the morning and, taking his bowl and robe, entered Kosambī for alms. ",
  "an7.43:1.4": "Then it occurred to him, ",
  "an7.43:1.5": "“It’s too early to wander for alms in Kosambī. ",
  "an7.43:1.6": "Why don’t I visit the monastery for the wanderers of other religions?” ",
  "an7.43:1.7": "Then he went to the monastery for the wanderers of other religions and exchanged greetings with the wanderers there. ",
  "an7.43:1.8": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he sat down to one side. ",
  "an7.43:2.1": "Now at that time while those wanderers of other religions were sitting together this discussion came up among them, ",
  "an7.43:2.2": "“Reverends, anyone who lives the full and pure spiritual life for twelve years is qualified to be called a ‘graduate mendicant’.” ",
  "an7.43:3.1": "Ānanda neither approved nor rejected that statement of the wanderers of other religions. ",
  "an7.43:3.2": "He rose from his seat, thinking, ",
  "an7.43:3.3": "“I will learn the meaning of this statement from the Buddha himself.” ",
  "an7.43:3.4": "Then Ānanda wandered for alms in Kosambī. After the meal, on his return from almsround, he went to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, and to